  "slug": "high-nanoantenna-b3b2",
  "summary": "Five preprints show resonant nano-photonic structures delivering UV harmonic enhancement, high-Q chirality, and record THz dynamic range.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is engineering resonances in sub-wavelength structures to enhance or control light-matter interaction across spectral regimes. Gold nano-pillar metasurfaces boost second and third harmonic generation into the UV and deep-UV. A coaxial plasmonic nanoantenna is mapped for inverse Faraday magnetization across gold, silver, copper, aluminum and TiN. A silicon BIC metasurface uses QBIC-GMR strong coupling to reach intrinsic circular dichroism of 0.995 with Q of 1083 at 1653.9 nm. Plasmonic nanoantenna arrays with hollow-core fiber coupling give polarization-resilient THz generation and detection, with 2.1 mW output and 145 dB dynamic range. Whispering gallery mode hybridization in high-index photonic molecules adds a tunable-coupling route. The new element is quantified performance via resonance and material design.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-18"
}
